{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Ah3HgjkdnwwaTXVP4zBZwA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility implementations), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build targets), `docs/` (specifications).\n\n**Current state**:\n- `pkg/sys/` — exists (source code present: stat.go, stat_darwin.go, stat_linux.go, terminal.go)\n- `pkg/format/` — exists (source code present: color.go, size.go, table.go)\n- `pkg/testutils/` — spec complete, **no source code on working branch**\n- `cmd/` — no utilities implemented on working branch\n- Code from earlier generation runs lives only at generation-merged tags, not on HEAD\n\n**Current release (00.0)** — \"Batch 0: foundational infrastructure\":\n- uc001-magefiles — magefiles/ excluded by DD7; cmd/version is the only valid target\n- uc002-format — **already exists** in source_code\n- uc003-sys — **already exists** in source_code\n- uc004-testutils — **not started, no source code** → this is the priority\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nWithin rel00.0, `pkg/format/` and `pkg/sys/` already exist as source code. `magefiles/` is excluded by DD7. The remaining gap is `pkg/testutils/` (rel00.0-uc004), the differential testing harness. This is foundational infrastructure — every utility's tests depend on it. It must be built before any `cmd/` package can be verified.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/testutils DiffTest struct and RunDiffTest -- rel00.0-uc004-testutils\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/testutils/ component description, data structures section for DiffTest definition, DD2 differential testing, DD6 LC_ALL=C constraint)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (find and read the testutils PRD -- file matching prd*testutils*.yaml -- to get exact requirement IDs and design choices)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc004-testutils.yaml (concrete execution path for the testing harness)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-00.0.yaml (test cases for rel00.0 use cases)\n      - pkg/sys/terminal.go (existing package conventions -- copyright header, comment style, import grouping)\n      - go.mod (module path for import references)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: create\n        note: DiffTest struct definition, RunDiffTest execution function, stdout/stderr/exit-code comparison, normalization hook support\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define a DiffTest struct with fields for: path to the Go binary under test, path to the reference GNU binary, command-line arguments ([]string), optional stdin input ([]byte or string), environment variables ([]string), and optional normalization functions for stdout and stderr. Match the data structure described in ARCHITECTURE.yaml: 'DiffTest: Go struct in pkg/testutils/ defining a single differential test case with fields for input arguments, stdin, environment, expected exit code, and expected output.'\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement a RunDiffTest function that accepts *testing.T and a DiffTest (or []DiffTest), executes both the Go binary and the reference binary with identical stdin, arguments, and environment using os/exec.Command, and captures stdout, stderr, and exit code from each execution.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Compare stdout, stderr, and exit code between the Go binary and reference binary. When a normalization function is provided on the DiffTest, apply it to both outputs before comparison. Report divergences via t.Errorf with the input that triggered the divergence, the expected output (reference binary), and the actual output (Go binary).\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Set LC_ALL=C in the environment for all differential test executions per ARCHITECTURE.yaml design decision DD6 (locale handling deferred). Merge LC_ALL=C with any environment variables specified in the DiffTest, with DiffTest env taking precedence if it also sets LC_ALL.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Primary source file is difftest.go, named after the primary exported type DiffTest. Do not name it testutils.go (project convention per ARCHITECTURE.yaml P7).\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use os/exec.Command to run both binaries. Capture stdout and stderr into bytes.Buffer. Extract exit code from exec.ExitError. A binary that exits 0 with no ExitError is exit code 0.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"DiffTest is a plain struct, not an interface. RunDiffTest is a package-level function. Normalization hooks are optional function fields (type func([]byte) []byte) on the DiffTest struct -- nil means no normalization (byte-for-byte comparison).\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Follow the copyright header and package doc comment conventions visible in pkg/sys/terminal.go. The package doc comment goes on difftest.go since it is the primary file.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/testutils/difftest.go exists and compiles without errors: go build ./pkg/testutils/... succeeds.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"DiffTest struct contains fields for Go binary path, reference binary path, arguments, stdin, environment, and normalization functions.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"RunDiffTest executes two binaries with identical inputs and compares stdout, stderr, and exit code.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Divergences are reported with the triggering input, expected output (reference), and actual output (Go binary).\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"LC_ALL=C is injected into every execution environment by default.\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/testutils/... passes with no warnings.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22067,"cache_read_input_tokens":19285,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22067},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2513428-7f6b-4a9b-b956-0a0269f654ab","uuid":"390f2a94-2185-4418-8285-80398e4ef516"}
